  "feedbackGuard": "Feedback suppression",
  "feedbackGuardBody": "For when the speaker is heard by the microphone. Echo cancellation removes what it can predict; these handle what is left, and they work in quite different ways.",
  "feedbackOff": "No feedback suppression",
  "feedbackOffBody": "Echo cancellation alone. Start here, and change it only if you hear yourself coming back or a howl builds up.",
  "feedbackDuck": "Turn the microphone down while others talk",
  "feedbackDuckBody": "What intercoms have always done, and the most effective with a speaker close to the microphone in a helmet. The cost is that talking over somebody becomes harder.",
  "feedbackHowl": "Cut only when a howl builds",
  "feedbackHowlBody": "Leaves ordinary conversation completely alone and cuts hard the moment a tone starts climbing. Does nothing about mild bleed.",
  "feedbackResidual": "Suppress whatever echo cancellation missed",
  "feedbackResidualBody": "Attenuates in proportion to how much of the sound looks like the far end rather than you. The gentlest on a real conversation, and the weakest against a genuine howl.",
  "dehiss": "Hiss removal",
  "dehissBody": "For the steady hiss a microphone adds under everything. Separate from noise suppression, which handles the road and the wind: those are loud and change with speed, while hiss is quiet, high and unvarying.",
  "dehissOff": "No hiss removal",
  "dehissOffBody": "Leaves the sound alone. Start here — both of the others discard something, and a link that already sounds fine is not worth changing.",
  "dehissExpander": "Turn quiet passages down further",
  "dehissExpanderBody": "Attenuates in proportion to how far below the noise floor the sound sits, so speech is untouched and the gaps between words go quiet. Cannot make a voice sound processed; can make the background breathe.",
  "dehissSpectral": "Learn the hiss and subtract it",
  "dehissSpectralBody": "Measures the noise while nobody is talking and removes it frequency by frequency, so hiss goes from under speech as well as from the gaps. The strongest option, and the one that can leave a faint flicker behind it.",
